# Block of Hemp Leaves — vanilla oak_leaves' own foliage noise, retoned to hemp.
#
# Same move as hemp_wool.mctex: the GRID below is vanilla `block/oak_leaves.png`
# extracted verbatim — four grey tones and the scatter of transparent gaps that make
# leaves read as leaves on Fancy. Redrawing that scatter by hand buys nothing and
# tiles worse. Only the PALETTE is ours.
#
# Vanilla's four greys were mapped by luminance onto the ramp between hemp_leaf.png's
# two body colours — 2F4C1C (shadow) and 73993B (highlight) — so every pixel is a
# colour the leaf item already uses and vanilla's shading spacing is preserved.
#
# It is deliberately NOT biome-tinted: the block is crafted, not grown, and a tint
# would have to be paired on the item side too (see crops.md). To retone, move the
# two endpoints and re-derive the middle two linearly by luminance.

@palette hemp_leaf
. = none
1 = 2F4C1C   from 686468
2 = 3C5A22   from 777577
3 = 587B2F   from 989998
4 = 73993B   from B9BCB9

@texture block/hemp_leaves 16x16 palette=hemp_leaf type=block tiling=true
11.4.33.2213..42
3...1123.323.434
..22.3324.3..444
.3211.4341....4.
3232..34...133..
332..42111..123.
22.14343.22.3324
211.444.1123.423
43.11433.2323.32
4...11123.333.43
.33.1.3324.3...4
4211...434.23...
233.33..4.1124.4
34.4211..1.34234
4.4343..22..434.
3.444..1112..4.3
